//
// SYNTHETIC SEED CORPUS — issue #89 (Slice 2b). Every merchant name and
// transaction below is INVENTED for testing the #88 harness end-to-end. None
// of it is drawn from any real user's account data, and it is NOT a real-world
// precision benchmark. See eval/CATEGORIZATION_CORPUS.md for the full format
// spec, methodology, and what a real corpus would need.
//
// A handful of entries deliberately reuse merchant keywords that already ship
// in finsight_core::categorize::KEYWORD_MAP (generic words like "pizza",
// "cafe", "parking", "pharmacy", "mortgage", plus a few widely-known public
// brand names like Costco/Netflix/Best Buy) so the REAL builtin matcher has
// something legitimate to hit — that is testing shipped code against its own
// public vocabulary, not fabricating a result. The majority of entries use
// wholly fictional merchant names with no keyword overlap, so honest coverage
// gaps show up in the baseline rather than being hidden.
//
// One entry ("Esso Corner Store", line g5t below is labelled groceries) is a
// deliberate TRAP: the builtin matcher's gas-station keyword will mis-fire as
// "transport" even though this purchase's ground truth is a convenience-store
// grocery run. This keeps the baseline honest — precision is not artificially
// 100%.
//
// Format: one JSON object per line. Lines starting with `//` or blank are
// skipped by the loader (mirrors eval/benchmark.jsonl's convention).
